<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/wenatchee.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/wenatchee-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/wenatchee.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/cities-we-serve/">Cities</a></li><li aria-current="page">Wenatchee</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">North Central Washington</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser for Wenatchee, WA</h1><p class="lede">Wenatchee sits where the Wenatchee River meets the Columbia, below dry, fire-prone foothills. The 2015 Sleepy Hollow Fire showed how quickly wildfire can reach neighborhoods here.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-y" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line light" href="/talk-to-an-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Chelan County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>North Central Washington</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose"><div class="note local"><b class="h">Local claim risks in Wenatchee</b><ul class="chips"><li>Wildfire</li><li>Snow load</li><li>Windstorms</li><li>Freeze</li><li>Smoke &amp; ash</li></ul><p class="housing"><b>Housing mix:</b> Older homes near downtown, foothill subdivisions, orchards and mountain cabins.</p></div>

<h2>Fire and snow country</h2>
<p>Wenatchee is the seat of Chelan County and the commercial center of North Central Washington, known for its apple orchards. The city sits at the base of dry foothills covered in grass and brush, where summer wildfires are a regular threat. In June 2015, the Sleepy Hollow Fire burned into the north end of Wenatchee and destroyed about 29 homes and several commercial buildings.</p>
<p>Winters can be snowy, especially in the hills and up the valley toward Leavenworth and Lake Wenatchee. Heavy snow loads can damage roofs, carports and outbuildings, and cold snaps can freeze pipes.</p>
<h2>Housing in the Wenatchee Valley</h2>
<p>Downtown Wenatchee has older homes. The foothills above town have newer subdivisions that sit right at the edge of open land. East Wenatchee across the river has a mix of homes and commercial buildings, and the valley has orchards, warehouses and cabins.</p>
<h2>Common Wenatchee claims</h2>
<ul>
<li>Wildfire total losses and smoke damage to surviving homes.</li>
<li>Snow-load damage to roofs and outbuildings.</li>
<li>Frozen pipes in cabins and second homes.</li>
<li>Wind damage to roofs and orchard structures.</li>
</ul>

